# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context for docker/hermes.Dockerfile.
#
# An ALLOWLIST, not a blocklist. This repository sits next to things that must
# never reach a Docker daemon: a real HF token in .env, the private sealed
# dataset under data/, and training runs under outputs/. With a blocklist, a new
# private file is included until someone remembers to exclude it; here nothing
# is included unless it is named below. Same posture as the upload allowlist in
# kleos_models.publishing.
#
# tests/test_container.py checks this file against every COPY in the
# Dockerfile, and checks that the private paths stay out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Exclude everything...
*

# ...then re-include exactly what the image needs.
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src
!scripts/_cli.py
!scripts/serve_hermes.py
!scripts/verify_deployment_package.py
!scripts/hermes_smoke.py
!configs/deployment/kleos_hermes_v006.yaml
!docker/requirements-hermes.txt

# Never, even inside a re-included directory.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
**/*.safetensors
**/*.bin
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.gguf
**/*.jsonl
**/.env
**/.env.*
